17] [17592186153199 #edb/ref 1061 3712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153199 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4dc61433-6c56-58c8-9a95-4614aa5f1bf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153199 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186153339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153200 #edb/ref 1061 3715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153200 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e8203c67-93c8-55d2-b5fd-7a7003ecaf79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153200 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153338 #edb/ref 1064 "How does a proportional relationship look when we plot it in the $(x,y)$ plane?\n\nTo answer this, let's consider the following proportional relationship:\n\n$$\ny = 2x\n$$\n\nTo plot a graph, we first need a table of values. \n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |\n| $1$ |  |\n| $2$ |  |\n| $3$ |  |\n\nFilling in the $y$-values using the equation $y = 2x,$ we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $2$ |\n| $2$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $6$ |\n\nSo, we have the following $(x,y)$ coordinates:\n\n$$\n(0,0), \\quad (1,2),  \\quad (2,4),  \\quad (3,6)\n$$\n\nIf we plot these points in the coordinate plane, we get the following:\n\n![](images/a8/a8cd951c66c67b8f28b791011c7553675b3112029d9ebe4b19769127b5e75bd5.png)\n\nThis leads us to the following important fact:\n\n*The graph of any proportional relationship is a straight line that passes through the origin $(0,0)$.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153338 #edb/ref 1065 1507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153338 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "becbb429-3b12-59c4-8172-aef250c47df9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153338 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153339 #edb/ref 1064 "When there is a proportional relationship between $x$ and $y,$ we can express this using the **proportionality symbol** $\\propto,$ as follows:\n\n$$\ny \\propto x\n$$\n\nNote that the following statements are all equivalent:\n\n- $y = kx$\n\n- $y$ **varies directly** with $x$\n\n- $y$ is **directly proportional** to $x$\n\n- $y \\propto x$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153339 #edb/ref 1065 1508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153339 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "503f0382-0b82-583d-898a-bc1dd1aa02d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153339 #edb/ref 1067 "Alternative Notations and Terminology" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497818 #edb/ref 1080 "II and IV only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497818 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497818 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07ec417b-980a-5d17-a5b9-12017396fe87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497839 #edb/ref 1080 "d=240t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497839 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497839 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10a9528e-1c2c-5770-b44f-a6e4d3c1e7a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497846 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{9}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497846 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497846 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14d25023-34e5-5862-8bea-4fc160f76af9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497886 #edb/ref 1080 "d=210t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497886 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497886 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "29f1ebd2-840a-5666-b57c-40488ad0dbbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497891 #edb/ref 1080 "d=100t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497891 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497891 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2bf3586b-e955-5c1c-9ff9-3fedb68db294" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497903 #edb/ref 1080 "None" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497903 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497903 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "31c5393e-18b4-501d-a2c9-6cf5bd7ff18c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497992 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\frac{5}{2}$ gallons per minute" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497992 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497992 #edb/ref 108